{{also|Tampon|tampón}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Tampon with applicator.jpg|thumb|A tampon with an applicator]]

===Etymology===
{{defdate|1848}} Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|tampon}}, from {{der|en|frm|tampion}}, a nasalised variant of {{m|frm|tapon}}, a diminutive or augmented form of {{der|en|fro|tape|t=plug, bung, tap}}, from {{der|en|frk|*tappo|t=stopper, plug}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*tappô|t=plug, tap}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|zapfo||stopper}}, {{cog|ang|tæppa||stopper}}. More at {{l|en|tap}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|[ˈtʰæmpɒn]}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tampon.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|[ˈtʰæmpɑn]}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[plug]] of [[cotton]] or other [[absorbent]] material [[inserted]] into a [[body cavity]] or wound to [[absorb]] fluid, especially one inserted in the [[vagina]] during [[menstruation]].
# A double-headed [[drumstick]] primarily for the [[bass drum]].
# An [[ink]]ing [[pad]] used in [[lithographic]] [[printing]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|intravaginal plug used to absorb menstrual blood}} {{l|en|vampire's teabag}} {{qualifier|slang}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|emotional tampon}}
* {{l|en|tampo}}
* {{l|en|tampography}}

